prompt.text:
Repair the following CommonJS module and return one corrected complete source file. It must export exactly `{ stableViewportHeight }`.

`stableViewportHeight(samples)` receives a non-empty array of positive finite numbers representing repeated viewport measurements. Return the numeric median after sorting a copy in ascending numeric order. For an even number of samples, return the arithmetic mean of the two middle values. Reject empty arrays and malformed values with `TypeError`. Do not mutate the input array. Duplicate and fractional measurements are valid.

Known-bad source:
```javascript
'use strict';

function stableViewportHeight(samples) {
  if (!Array.isArray(samples) || samples.length === 0 ||
      samples.some(value => typeof value !== 'number' || !Number.isFinite(value) || value <= 0)) {
    throw new TypeError('samples must contain positive finite numbers');
  }
  const ordered = samples.slice().sort();
  const middle = Math.floor(ordered.length / 2);
  return ordered.length % 2 === 1
    ? ordered[middle]
    : (ordered[middle - 1] + ordered[middle]) / 2;
}

module.exports = { stableViewportHeight };
```

Return only the complete source file; do not include Markdown fences or prose.

